  "payload": {
    "rawResponseText": "For an **upper-upscale** hotel project in the Caribbean and Latin America, owners and developers most commonly shortlist the major international groups with active regional pipelines and brand portfolios in that segment: **Hilton**, **Marriott**, **IHG**, **Hyatt**, and, in some markets, **Choice/Radisson** and **Wyndham** through their upper-upscale or conversion-friendly brands.[3][5][6][7][8]\n\nThe brands most often seen in that shortlist are typically:\n\n- **Hilton** — especially **Curio Collection**, **Tapestry Collection**, and sometimes **DoubleTree by Hilton** for upper-upscale positioning and conversions.[6][8]\n- **Marriott** — especially **Westin**, **Autograph Collection**, **The Luxury Collection**, **Ritz-Carlton**, and in some cases **JW Marriott** or **Sheraton** depending on the asset and market.[2][9][10]\n- **IHG** — particularly **InterContinental**, **Kimpton**, and **Hotel Indigo** for lifestyle or resort-led upper-upscale projects.[3]\n- **Hyatt** — especially **Hyatt Regency**, **Andaz**, **Thompson**, and **Alila** where the project leans more lifestyle or luxury-upper-upscale.[3]\n- **Choice/Radisson** — usually through **Radisson Red** or other internationally recognized brands in select LATAM markets.[5]\n- **Wyndham** — less dominant in the pure upper-upscale resort space, but still relevant in some mixed-use or conversion opportunities via premium brands.[3]\n\nIf you want, I can also narrow this to:\n- **resort vs. urban**\n- **all-inclusive vs. EP/BB**\n- **best-fit brands by country** in the Caribbean or Latin America",
